Package: yourhonor
Title: Calibrate Large Language Model Judges
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jay", "Clark", , "27960665+JsizzleR@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Treat a large language model used as an evaluator (an
    "LLM-as-judge") as a measurement instrument and report its
    psychometric properties. Given a judge and a set of human-labeled
    examples, 'yourhonor' reports chance-corrected agreement between the
    judge and humans with bootstrap confidence intervals: Cohen's kappa
    (Cohen 1960) <doi:10.1177/001316446002000104>, Krippendorff's alpha
    (Hayes and Krippendorff 2007) <doi:10.1080/19312450709336664>, and
    Gwet's AC1 (Gwet 2008) <doi:10.1348/000711006X126600> and weighted
    AC2 (Gwet 2014, ISBN:978-0970806284). It also reports human-human
    reliability when several raters are supplied, per-class error
    intervals, structured paired bias probes and test-retest stability.
    Explicit acceptance policies turn evidence into conservative
    decisions, and versioned artifacts support portable aggregate audit
    review. It complements the 'ellmer' and 'vitals' evaluation stack: it
    does not run evaluations, it measures the judge that scores them.
